# Copy to .env.local (which git ignores) and fill in.

# Optional. Google Books fills in page counts, genres and book heights that
# Open Library is missing. Without a key, requests share a tiny public quota
# and usually fail, and the app falls back to Open Library alone.
# Get a key at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials (enable "Books API").
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_BOOKS_API_KEY=

# Optional. Where the app finds the Bookie API (accounts, sync, friends). The web app uses its own address (/api), so
# leave this empty there, except to point the Expo dev server at a local API (`npm run api:dev`, then
# http://localhost:8788, with ALLOWED_ORIGINS in .dev.vars). The phone app defaults to https://mybookie.pages.dev;
# use https://staging.mybookie.pages.dev to test against staging.
EXPO_PUBLIC_BOOKIE_API_URL=
